1
00:00:01,251 --> 00:00:03,750
(Episode 4)

2
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:16,860
Ms. Choi, please.

3
00:00:22,450 --> 00:00:25,845
Hold on. Just hear me out.

4
00:00:26,193 --> 00:00:27,193
Hello?

5
00:00:28,283 --> 00:00:29,325
Hello?

6
00:00:32,370 --> 00:00:33,462
Ms. Choi.

7
00:00:35,488 --> 00:00:38,010
Did you meet your first love
in your hometown yesterday?

8
00:00:40,658 --> 00:00:41,997
What is your real name?

9
00:00:42,459 --> 00:00:44,053
What is the name of your first love?

10
00:00:46,258 --> 00:00:47,258
Tree.

11
00:00:47,681 --> 00:00:49,923
Eun Seo. Choi Eun Seo.

12
00:00:51,715 --> 00:00:52,876
You look beautiful.

13
00:00:52,876 --> 00:00:54,424
Jun Seo, come this way, too.

14
00:00:57,147 --> 00:00:59,464
Congratulations. I can't believe
you have grown up to get married.

15
00:00:59,464 --> 00:01:01,457
He is gorgeous.

16
00:01:08,455 --> 00:01:09,752
Isn't there a reward for me today?

17
00:01:09,752 --> 00:01:11,049
I do have something for you.

18
00:01:11,049 --> 00:01:13,080
But please wait until the party is over.

19
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:16,631
When is the party over?

20
00:01:16,631 --> 00:01:17,934
Are we not done yet?

21
00:01:17,934 --> 00:01:20,784
No way. We still have so much to do.

22
00:01:20,784 --> 00:01:23,783
We'll drop our parents off at home first,

23
00:01:23,783 --> 00:01:25,700
have dinner with our cousins,

24
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:28,489
and also send thank you cards out
to the guests who came today.

25
00:01:30,292 --> 00:01:31,377
I can't do that.

26
00:01:32,693 --> 00:01:33,743
Let's get out of here.

27
00:01:47,086 --> 00:01:48,252
You there.

28
00:01:48,252 --> 00:01:49,289
Yes, sir.

29
00:01:49,781 --> 00:01:51,661
How dare you look straight into my eyes!

30
00:01:53,618 --> 00:01:55,915
What? Do you have two children? You?

31
00:01:56,848 --> 00:01:58,082
Yes, sir.

32
00:01:58,082 --> 00:02:01,292
I said I have two children,
but didn't say they were my children.

33
00:02:03,095 --> 00:02:04,131
You.

34
00:02:04,131 --> 00:02:05,204
Yes, sir.

35
00:02:06,248 --> 00:02:08,978
You said you were 37 years old,
didn't you?

36
00:02:09,763 --> 00:02:11,005
Yes, I did.

37
00:02:11,707 --> 00:02:12,930
What?

38
00:02:12,930 --> 00:02:15,041
You always flirt with women, so...

39
00:02:15,041 --> 00:02:17,851
I got worried,
and told you I was 37 years old.

40
00:02:17,851 --> 00:02:18,851
Is there a problem?

41
00:02:20,931 --> 00:02:22,683
I do not think you can blame me.

42
00:02:22,683 --> 00:02:24,945
If I had told you I was 22 years old,

43
00:02:24,945 --> 00:02:26,229
would you have left me alone?

44
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:33,514
We are not allowed to have chats
with guests during work.

45
00:02:33,514 --> 00:02:34,941
Have a good day.

46
00:02:37,610 --> 00:02:38,757
By the way,

47
00:02:39,250 --> 00:02:43,466
it has been fun and intriguing
to observe your complicated relationships.

48
00:02:43,466 --> 00:02:47,114
But women do not like that.

49
00:02:47,114 --> 00:02:48,179
That.

50
00:02:52,474 --> 00:02:54,029
These pants don't even have a zipper.

51
00:03:10,018 --> 00:03:12,740
Is it bright? Is the light bright enough?

52
00:03:14,986 --> 00:03:16,745
Is it for my solo exhibition?

53
00:03:16,745 --> 00:03:19,298
You said you would move
to a new work studio.

54
00:03:19,298 --> 00:03:22,570
You can work here.

55
00:03:22,570 --> 00:03:24,820
This is your prize and my engagement gift.

56
00:03:26,202 --> 00:03:28,203
Is this your engagement gift?

57
00:03:29,082 --> 00:03:32,442
It was not that easy
to move everything here alone.

58
00:03:32,442 --> 00:03:35,132
That was why I didn't say anything
about you going to your hometown.

59
00:03:35,730 --> 00:03:40,220
Why did you move my stuff without asking?

60
00:03:41,235 --> 00:03:42,385
Are you upset?

61
00:03:42,385 --> 00:03:44,372
No, I am not, but...

62
00:03:46,178 --> 00:03:48,395
This is too much to take as a gift.

63
00:03:48,395 --> 00:03:50,137
You needn't feel that way.

64
00:03:50,137 --> 00:03:53,634
This place has been empty
since I bought it.

65
00:03:53,634 --> 00:03:54,928
You can work here...

66
00:03:54,928 --> 00:03:57,293
and it would be our temporary home
until the wedding.

67
00:03:57,293 --> 00:04:01,378
But still, who gives a house
as an engagement gift?

68
00:04:01,378 --> 00:04:03,160
Besides, I am going to Sokcho soon.

69
00:04:03,902 --> 00:04:05,701
Do you remember Ji Hwan in Sokcho?

70
00:04:05,701 --> 00:04:07,549
He rented an abandoned school.

71
00:04:07,549 --> 00:04:09,798
So, I will help with his work there,

72
00:04:09,798 --> 00:04:11,842
and I will also teach classes
at a university nearby.

73
00:04:13,070 --> 00:04:15,487
You should've told me.

74
00:04:15,487 --> 00:04:17,746
You should've told me before you did this.

75
00:04:18,969 --> 00:04:21,427
It must've been a lot of work
to move everything.

76
00:04:22,281 --> 00:04:23,834
What a waste.

77
00:04:51,284 --> 00:04:52,424
Ms. Choi, please.

78
00:04:53,692 --> 00:04:55,713
Yes, sir. I will connect you with her.

79
00:05:06,652 --> 00:05:07,965
Hello?

80
00:05:07,965 --> 00:05:11,046
You know that.
You know what types of girls I'm into.

81
00:05:11,046 --> 00:05:12,924
You know I have pretty high standards.

82
00:05:12,924 --> 00:05:15,319
I'm not a Casanova who goes for any girl.

83
00:05:15,319 --> 00:05:16,319
What are you doing?

84
00:05:16,319 --> 00:05:19,017
Ms. Choi? No way!

85
00:05:19,017 --> 00:05:21,556
She is not even close to my type.

86
00:05:22,641 --> 00:05:24,257
My types are...

87
00:05:24,257 --> 00:05:25,752
Catherine Zeta-Jones when the girl
is sitting down,

88
00:05:25,752 --> 00:05:28,632
Claudia Schiffer when the girl
is standing up.

89
00:05:28,632 --> 00:05:30,897
But, she is very short...

90
00:05:30,897 --> 00:05:33,209
and looks like an old lady.

91
00:05:33,209 --> 00:05:34,747
But, she said she was 22 years old.

92
00:05:34,747 --> 00:05:36,515
That can't be true. That is a lie.

93
00:05:36,515 --> 00:05:38,517
That is an absolute lie.

94
00:05:39,231 --> 00:05:42,192
Han Tae Seok. What are you talking about?

95
00:05:43,796 --> 00:05:46,102
Why did you call me and talk about a girl?

96
00:05:49,443 --> 00:05:51,596
Don't you even want to hear about me?

97
00:05:51,596 --> 00:05:54,941
- About what?
- My engagement party.

98
00:05:54,941 --> 00:05:56,272
Don't you want to know how it went?

99
00:05:57,357 --> 00:05:58,972
- What are you doing?
- Right.

100
00:05:58,972 --> 00:06:00,423
Yoon Jun Seo.

101
00:06:02,041 --> 00:06:03,124
Okay, congratulations.

102
00:06:03,124 --> 00:06:05,755
Thank you.

103
00:06:05,755 --> 00:06:08,946
I am coming soon. See you then.

104
00:06:08,946 --> 00:06:10,541
Thank you.

105
00:06:11,538 --> 00:06:12,757
Yes, this is the operator.

106
00:06:18,688 --> 00:06:20,027
My engagement party.

107
00:06:24,215 --> 00:06:28,579
An engagement party? Is he a friend?

108
00:06:29,508 --> 00:06:31,740
How is my father?

109
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:35,757
Yes, he is well.
His wife's birthday is next week.

110
00:06:35,757 --> 00:06:36,993
You are coming, right?

111
00:06:45,359 --> 00:06:47,168
Would they be pleased if I did?

112
00:06:48,632 --> 00:06:51,311
Give it to me. Where do I need to sign?

113
00:06:51,311 --> 00:06:52,530
Right here, please.

114
00:06:53,272 --> 00:06:56,394
It's a regular personnel realignment
held every three months.

115
00:07:01,255 --> 00:07:02,994
What is a personal maid?

116
00:07:03,816 --> 00:07:05,134
Well.

117
00:07:05,134 --> 00:07:07,911
It is a service for VIP guests...

118
00:07:09,475 --> 00:07:11,799
Do you need a personal maid?

119
00:07:25,197 --> 00:07:26,332
What is this?

120
00:07:26,332 --> 00:07:28,372
How come an operator switches
to a maid so suddenly?

121
00:07:28,372 --> 00:07:30,223
How could this happen?

122
00:07:31,429 --> 00:07:35,950
Have you heard that the youngest son
of the CEO is staying here?

123
00:07:37,372 --> 00:07:38,934
Then, is he...

124
00:07:41,828 --> 00:07:46,131
The troublemaker whom the president
and the CEO have given up on.

125
00:07:46,131 --> 00:07:47,639
Just give him whatever he wants.

126
00:07:49,427 --> 00:07:51,477
He is also a womanizer, so...

127
00:07:51,477 --> 00:07:54,621
the reason he specifically
chose this girl is...

128
00:07:54,621 --> 00:07:57,385
Are you saying the girl has issues?

129
00:07:58,779 --> 00:08:01,686
Who knows? They might like each other...

130
00:08:04,411 --> 00:08:06,455
When did he have time to seduce her?

131
00:08:10,819 --> 00:08:14,858
I was so nervous because I didn't expect
we'd be in the same department.

132
00:08:14,858 --> 00:08:16,287
I was surprised when you walked in.

133
00:08:16,287 --> 00:08:18,417
- Didn't you recognize me?
- No, I didn't.

134
00:08:18,417 --> 00:08:19,741
How lucky to get in the same department?

135
00:08:39,829 --> 00:08:40,829
Choi Eun Seo?

136
00:08:42,764 --> 00:08:45,435
I am Manager Kim Moon Jung.

137
00:08:45,435 --> 00:08:48,507
I will manage and supervise
your work from now on,

138
00:08:48,507 --> 00:08:51,256
so please discuss any issues,
even trivial ones, with me.

139
00:08:52,556 --> 00:08:54,970
Since housekeeping is the job...

140
00:08:54,970 --> 00:08:57,268
that serves guests in the closest way,

141
00:08:57,268 --> 00:09:00,665
your sincerity will determine
the impression of our hotel.

142
00:09:00,665 --> 00:09:02,435
Always pay attention to the guests.

143
00:09:02,435 --> 00:09:07,211
However, personal relationships
with guests are never allowed.

144
00:09:07,211 --> 00:09:10,748
You will be fired no matter what,
under the company policy.

145
00:09:11,852 --> 00:09:13,524
Do you understand, Choi Eun Seo?

146
00:09:20,538 --> 00:09:23,842
A personal maid? What is this all about?

147
00:09:23,842 --> 00:09:25,273
Don't pretend you can't hear me.

148
00:09:25,273 --> 00:09:27,691
This pool has an audio system underwater.

149
00:09:28,272 --> 00:09:31,329
I am an operator, not even
a full-time employee at this hotel.

150
00:09:31,329 --> 00:09:33,443
What do people think about this?

151
00:09:34,695 --> 00:09:37,583
My manager already has
a bad impression of me.

152
00:09:37,583 --> 00:09:39,969
I will be fired if people think
I am in a relationship with the guest.

153
00:09:39,969 --> 00:09:41,457
Will you take responsibility
if that happens?

154
00:09:41,457 --> 00:09:42,914
Will you take responsibility?

155
00:09:50,031 --> 00:09:52,970
Take responsibility? How would I do that?

156
00:09:55,338 --> 00:09:56,699
How would I do that?

157
00:09:59,143 --> 00:10:01,328
I apologize, sir.

158
00:10:01,328 --> 00:10:04,380
For a moment, I thought we could talk.
I overestimated you.

159
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:09,600
Having a conversation is only possible
between humans.

160
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:10,634
What?

161
00:10:12,224 --> 00:10:13,840
Get prepared for it.

162
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:17,288
I will call room services days and nights.

163
00:10:17,288 --> 00:10:18,890
So you had better get ready.

164
00:10:42,081 --> 00:10:45,336
Jun Seo, I heard when you were in Korea...

165
00:10:45,336 --> 00:10:47,884
you used to draw a lot of portraits
in middle school.

166
00:10:49,505 --> 00:10:52,092
But why haven't you painted me?

167
00:10:54,657 --> 00:10:57,789
You are too beautiful.
You are too beautiful for me to paint.

168
00:11:01,584 --> 00:11:02,584
What is it?

169
00:11:03,634 --> 00:11:04,848
Yes?

170
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:09,638
This is a place near the school
where I am going to stay.

171
00:11:09,638 --> 00:11:12,370
So it is close to your hometown.

172
00:11:13,975 --> 00:11:16,130
Did you use to go there often
when you were young?

173
00:11:16,766 --> 00:11:19,999
No, just once with my sister.

174
00:11:19,999 --> 00:11:21,179
Did you go with Sin Ae?

175
00:11:22,952 --> 00:11:25,163
No, I didn't go with her.

176
00:11:26,296 --> 00:11:28,695
I went there with my cousin.

177
00:11:28,695 --> 00:11:29,930
Your cousin?

178
00:11:30,672 --> 00:11:32,138
What did you do?

179
00:11:32,838 --> 00:11:34,361
We just hung out.

180
00:11:35,247 --> 00:11:38,522
I drew her face here this big,
and we just hung out.

181
00:11:39,926 --> 00:11:43,332
She was probably not as pretty as I am,
so you drew her.

182
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:48,282
No, she was not.

183
00:11:49,449 --> 00:11:52,046
What is she doing now?

184
00:11:52,046 --> 00:11:53,046
What?

185
00:11:53,557 --> 00:11:57,029
I lost contact with her
since leaving for the U.S.

186
00:11:57,029 --> 00:12:01,003
I have been looking for her
since I came back last year.

187
00:12:01,003 --> 00:12:02,428
I heard she moved to Seoul.

188
00:12:03,196 --> 00:12:04,494
You said she was your cousin.

189
00:12:05,219 --> 00:12:07,374
She is a distant relative.

190
00:12:09,372 --> 00:12:13,028
I will go to Sokcho again next week
before the move.

191
00:12:13,028 --> 00:12:14,933
I will also stop by the school.

192
00:12:14,933 --> 00:12:17,686
I will go with you. I miss Tae Seok, too.

193
00:12:18,972 --> 00:12:21,180
You can come next time when I am moving.

194
00:12:21,180 --> 00:12:24,349
Tae Seok will come to Seoul that day
for his mother's birthday.

195
00:12:27,139 --> 00:12:31,750
By the way, he is being more patient
than we thought.

196
00:12:36,944 --> 00:12:39,087
Ms. Choi, I am hungry.

197
00:12:39,087 --> 00:12:40,977
You have three minutes, okay?

198
00:12:40,977 --> 00:12:42,130
I will time you.

199
00:14:40,008 --> 00:14:41,595
What is this?

200
00:15:00,881 --> 00:15:01,932
Did you want to see me?

201
00:15:05,936 --> 00:15:07,637
Did you lose something?

202
00:15:07,637 --> 00:15:08,887
Yes. I lost my watch.

203
00:15:09,661 --> 00:15:12,393
I am going to Seoul this evening
for my mother's birthday.

204
00:15:13,853 --> 00:15:15,386
Have you seen my watch here?

205
00:15:16,366 --> 00:15:18,113
It was there.

206
00:15:18,782 --> 00:15:20,526
Did you really see it here?

207
00:15:20,526 --> 00:15:22,169
When I was cleaning out the trash...

208
00:15:23,615 --> 00:15:24,625
Is it with trash?

209
00:15:40,847 --> 00:15:44,629
How could you make such a mistake?
I can't believe it.

210
00:15:44,629 --> 00:15:45,878
What are we doing here?

211
00:15:47,139 --> 00:15:48,533
What is wrong with me?

212
00:15:48,533 --> 00:15:50,643
Why do I have so much bad luck?

213
00:15:50,643 --> 00:15:52,894
I had enough trouble
with a watch a long time ago.

214
00:15:57,909 --> 00:15:58,943
Eun Seo.

215
00:16:00,260 --> 00:16:03,101
No. I didn't do it.

216
00:16:03,101 --> 00:16:04,544
I didn't.

217
00:16:06,164 --> 00:16:08,181
It's not here.

218
00:16:08,181 --> 00:16:09,992
When do we dig up all of them?

219
00:16:31,738 --> 00:16:34,892
I could not find your watch. I am sorry.

220
00:16:36,025 --> 00:16:38,485
For now, please take this
for your convenience.

221
00:16:43,338 --> 00:16:46,738
I am not sure how much your watch costs...

222
00:16:46,738 --> 00:16:47,949
About 2,400 dollars?

223
00:16:49,842 --> 00:16:50,842
Or 3,200 dollars?

224
00:16:51,954 --> 00:16:53,643
Did you say 2,400 dollars
or 3,200 dollars?

225
00:16:56,167 --> 00:16:57,962
But, what can we do here?

226
00:17:00,808 --> 00:17:02,335
You found your watch!

227
00:17:02,335 --> 00:17:03,841
You actually found it!

228
00:17:12,759 --> 00:17:13,759
So was that...?

229
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:15,595
Thanks for the great pizza.

230
00:17:18,350 --> 00:17:20,513
That was a joke, of course.

231
00:17:25,270 --> 00:17:26,949
Was it a joke?

232
00:17:26,949 --> 00:17:28,392
Are you saying that was a joke?

233
00:17:30,031 --> 00:17:33,114
I had to dig up all the trash
at the dumpsite to look for it.

234
00:17:33,114 --> 00:17:34,626
And you're saying it was a joke?

235
00:17:37,068 --> 00:17:38,725
People like you...

236
00:17:39,329 --> 00:17:41,148
I hate people like you so much.

237
00:17:47,994 --> 00:17:51,429
I am sorry, sir. Excuse me for now.

238
00:18:23,010 --> 00:18:24,030
Choi Eun Seo.

239
00:18:24,997 --> 00:18:27,396
Where are you going?
You are still on the clock.

240
00:18:27,396 --> 00:18:29,125
Have you moved into
staff accommodations, yet?

241
00:18:30,061 --> 00:18:32,997
That is why I am going home now
to pick up my stuff.

242
00:18:35,317 --> 00:18:36,713
Be careful about what you do.

243
00:18:38,976 --> 00:18:42,703
Because of people like you who think
everything is so fancy at a hotel,

244
00:18:42,703 --> 00:18:45,323
all hardworking hotel staff gets blamed.

245
00:18:47,352 --> 00:18:48,483
Please take it back.

246
00:18:51,359 --> 00:18:54,906
Please take it back.
I have not done anything to get blamed.

247
00:19:00,271 --> 00:19:02,100
How dare you look straight into my eyes!

248
00:19:02,100 --> 00:19:03,995
How shameless you are.

249
00:19:03,995 --> 00:19:05,869
Haven't you done anything to get blamed?

250
00:19:05,869 --> 00:19:08,821
People saw you pouring water
on the guest at the restaurant.

251
00:19:08,821 --> 00:19:10,494
Are you dating at work?

252
00:19:11,541 --> 00:19:12,908
Watch your behavior.

253
00:19:12,908 --> 00:19:16,604
If I hear about such a thing again,
I will do everything to fire you.

254
00:19:18,172 --> 00:19:20,726
You just try to be an overnight princess.

255
00:19:41,144 --> 00:19:42,738
She is still young.

256
00:19:42,738 --> 00:19:44,803
She's not that young, Mom.

257
00:19:44,803 --> 00:19:46,538
You bastard.

258
00:19:46,538 --> 00:19:49,112
- Why are you doing this to me?
- You...

259
00:19:52,276 --> 00:19:55,834
President Kim,
why don't we set a date now?

260
00:19:57,025 --> 00:19:58,166
No, it's fine.

261
00:19:59,090 --> 00:20:03,241
Your sister doesn't seem to be home today,
so I will come again later.

262
00:20:04,910 --> 00:20:07,221
Take this back, please.

263
00:20:07,221 --> 00:20:09,070
No.

264
00:20:09,070 --> 00:20:11,798
Please take them.
It is from my fishing boat.

265
00:20:11,798 --> 00:20:13,647
I will come by later.

266
00:20:17,109 --> 00:20:18,594
You, go away.

267
00:20:18,594 --> 00:20:19,765
All right.

268
00:20:19,765 --> 00:20:21,112
President Kim.

269
00:21:00,928 --> 00:21:03,828
Why do you have to live
in staff accommodations?

270
00:21:05,089 --> 00:21:07,381
I can come home once a week.

271
00:21:08,385 --> 00:21:10,290
Mom, eat it.

272
00:21:19,020 --> 00:21:20,677
President Kim...

273
00:21:22,739 --> 00:21:25,346
brought fish again today.

274
00:21:27,810 --> 00:21:30,494
I hate that he wants you, but...

275
00:21:32,817 --> 00:21:37,987
he bailed out your brother several times
from being locked up.

276
00:21:38,994 --> 00:21:40,332
Even this store...

277
00:21:42,306 --> 00:21:44,073
No, never mind.

278
00:21:44,073 --> 00:21:45,852
I am losing my mind.

279
00:22:01,859 --> 00:22:03,356
I am sorry, mom.

280
00:22:04,969 --> 00:22:11,396
But, please let me stay with you
a little longer.

281
00:22:14,250 --> 00:22:17,068
If I work as I am doing now,
I will get my savings next year.

282
00:22:18,671 --> 00:22:20,210
Then we will pay off the debt,

283
00:22:21,359 --> 00:22:23,242
and then change our address legally.

284
00:22:25,319 --> 00:22:26,478
Mom,

285
00:22:28,681 --> 00:22:31,094
please let me live with you
a little longer.

286
00:22:34,146 --> 00:22:35,246
I'm sorry.

287
00:22:37,123 --> 00:22:41,564
If I knew this would happen,
I should've sent you away then.

288
00:22:43,090 --> 00:22:44,814
Mom.

289
00:23:54,768 --> 00:23:55,803
Jun Seo.

290
00:24:01,536 --> 00:24:02,634
Jun Seo.

291
00:24:26,060 --> 00:24:27,599
What do you think?
Do you think you like it here?

292
00:24:29,156 --> 00:24:31,934
Yes, I like it a lot.

293
00:24:33,067 --> 00:24:35,453
My classes in Seoul were done last week.

294
00:24:35,453 --> 00:24:37,004
Should I move right away?

295
00:24:37,004 --> 00:24:38,452
I would like that.

296
00:24:38,452 --> 00:24:40,349
The duty of leaving this place empty...

297
00:24:40,349 --> 00:24:42,718
and going back home
to please Mom bothers me.

298
00:24:43,476 --> 00:24:47,196
Have you discussed things
with Yu Mi, though?

299
00:24:47,196 --> 00:24:48,339
I have.

300
00:24:48,339 --> 00:24:50,524
If I stay here, she can come here often.

301
00:24:50,524 --> 00:24:52,471
That would be good for her health.

302
00:24:52,471 --> 00:24:55,293
Right, you said she is not well.

303
00:24:58,660 --> 00:24:59,956
By the way, are you going somewhere?

304
00:24:59,956 --> 00:25:03,692
Yes, there is an interesting place,
so I will take some pictures.

305
00:25:03,692 --> 00:25:05,769
You should come with me.

306
00:25:13,957 --> 00:25:18,212
Are you taking pictures of squid?
What are you doing?

307
00:25:18,212 --> 00:25:21,920
I am taking photos of the village
through this gap.

308
00:25:24,555 --> 00:25:25,807
I see.

309
00:25:31,892 --> 00:25:34,501
You keep taking your pictures.
I will go over there to look around.

310
00:25:34,501 --> 00:25:35,582
All right.

311
00:26:48,549 --> 00:26:49,692
Ji Hwan.

312
00:27:27,088 --> 00:27:29,248
Aren't there any good ones?

313
00:27:29,248 --> 00:27:31,515
I've got a good one. Where is it?

314
00:27:33,430 --> 00:27:34,945
Yes, I have it here.

315
00:27:50,454 --> 00:27:51,454
Who is it?

316
00:27:55,901 --> 00:27:57,479
You haven't left for Seoul, yet.

317
00:27:57,479 --> 00:27:59,973
What are you doing here
early in the morning?

318
00:27:59,973 --> 00:28:01,408
Can I stay here for a couple of days?

319
00:28:05,774 --> 00:28:07,241
- It is the key.
- Yes.

320
00:28:08,124 --> 00:28:09,199
Here is your cell phone.

321
00:28:10,285 --> 00:28:12,719
You can ask the front desk
to charge your cell phone.

322
00:28:12,719 --> 00:28:15,015
What is going on, anyway?

323
00:28:16,075 --> 00:28:17,902
I think I might see someone I know.

324
00:28:19,067 --> 00:28:20,940
Did you see someone you know? Who?

325
00:28:22,500 --> 00:28:23,500
Well,

326
00:28:26,580 --> 00:28:29,359
I'll tell you later.
I'll tell you when I find her.

327
00:28:30,796 --> 00:28:33,289
You have many secrets these days.

328
00:28:35,158 --> 00:28:36,910
All right.
I'll see you when I get back from Seoul.

329
00:28:36,910 --> 00:28:38,246
It'll take two or three days.

330
00:28:38,246 --> 00:28:40,096
Until then, use whatever you want.

331
00:28:41,039 --> 00:28:43,473
And...

332
00:28:44,574 --> 00:28:47,630
you can't get close to my room attendant.

333
00:28:47,630 --> 00:28:50,489
I know I don't need to warn you,
cause you are such a gentleman.

334
00:28:51,245 --> 00:28:52,475
What about your room attendant?

335
00:28:53,375 --> 00:28:54,386
Is it a woman?

336
00:28:55,734 --> 00:28:57,005
Did you get back to your tricks here?

337
00:28:57,005 --> 00:28:58,458
Yes, just playing around.

338
00:28:59,488 --> 00:29:02,483
Hey, I don't think that's true.

339
00:29:02,990 --> 00:29:04,521
Give me your cell phone.

340
00:29:05,046 --> 00:29:06,434
What is she like?

341
00:29:07,551 --> 00:29:08,961
Just wait here.

342
00:29:13,311 --> 00:29:14,411
I'm just playing around.

343
00:29:29,665 --> 00:29:31,426
I told you
I was going to my parents in Seoul.

344
00:29:32,090 --> 00:29:33,441
I am on my way.

345
00:29:36,397 --> 00:29:39,557
It's my friend's cell phone. Charge it.

346
00:29:39,557 --> 00:29:41,594
My friend will stay in my room
for a couple of days.

347
00:29:54,942 --> 00:29:58,223
What do you think about this watch?
Do you like it?

348
00:29:58,223 --> 00:30:00,069
I will put on this instead.

349
00:30:00,069 --> 00:30:03,039
Someone gave it to me
and I like it more than mine.

350
00:30:03,039 --> 00:30:04,342
It has a stopwatch.

351
00:30:04,342 --> 00:30:07,503
Look, you can see the date, too.

352
00:30:07,503 --> 00:30:09,376
Do you want to see it? Look.

353
00:30:10,452 --> 00:30:11,625
It has a light on.

354
00:30:18,582 --> 00:30:21,256
I am sorry about earlier.

355
00:30:26,039 --> 00:30:27,039
See you later.

356
00:30:42,746 --> 00:30:44,594
- Sorry for keeping you waiting.
- That's all right.

357
00:30:45,638 --> 00:30:46,691
Let's go.

358
00:30:50,933 --> 00:30:52,688
- Hello.
- Yes, hi.

359
00:30:55,805 --> 00:30:58,417
Is the number 0215?

360
00:32:40,760 --> 00:32:42,589
It is fully charged.

361
00:32:42,589 --> 00:32:44,359
I was told you were going to stay
for a couple of days.

362
00:32:44,359 --> 00:32:47,783
I put your sleepwear in the closet
since there was no luggage.

363
00:32:48,726 --> 00:32:50,815
You received several messages.

364
00:32:57,213 --> 00:32:58,892
Jun Seo, it is me.

365
00:32:58,892 --> 00:33:01,101
I wonder why you haven't called me.

366
00:33:04,357 --> 00:33:06,724
I got your message.

367
00:33:06,724 --> 00:33:09,396
Whom are you looking for?

368
00:33:09,396 --> 00:33:11,916
Could you call me back to tell me more?

369
00:33:17,642 --> 00:33:18,936
If you need anything,

370
00:33:18,936 --> 00:33:23,300
my pager number is 012-323-0215.

371
00:33:23,300 --> 00:33:24,464
The number is 0215.

372
00:33:26,291 --> 00:33:27,903
It is the same number as mine.

373
00:34:05,119 --> 00:34:07,153
Thank you so much, Ji Hwan.

374
00:34:07,943 --> 00:34:09,225
But still.

375
00:34:10,328 --> 00:34:12,225
She is an acquaintance of mine.

376
00:34:12,960 --> 00:34:13,996
Yes.

377
00:34:14,921 --> 00:34:15,921
Yes.

378
00:34:19,099 --> 00:34:20,197
Hello?

379
00:34:20,921 --> 00:34:24,457
Ji Hwan, you are breaking up.
My phone is out of battery.

380
00:34:24,457 --> 00:34:25,548
Hello.

381
00:34:26,034 --> 00:34:27,859
Ji Hwan, I will call you back later.

382
00:34:56,145 --> 00:34:57,156
Hello.

383
00:34:57,904 --> 00:34:58,943
Hello.

384
00:34:59,833 --> 00:35:00,895
Yes,

385
00:35:02,947 --> 00:35:05,101
Is this the guest in the villa?

386
00:35:05,988 --> 00:35:07,317
Did you page me?

387
00:35:07,317 --> 00:35:08,641
Yes, I...

388
00:35:10,135 --> 00:35:11,390
Hello?

389
00:35:11,390 --> 00:35:14,223
I would like to charge my cell phone.

390
00:35:14,223 --> 00:35:16,649
Of course, you can ask at the front desk.

391
00:35:18,222 --> 00:35:20,609
Okay, thanks.

392
00:35:30,862 --> 00:35:32,097
- I...
- So...

393
00:35:33,207 --> 00:35:35,315
What brought you here?

394
00:35:37,544 --> 00:35:39,055
Excuse me.

395
00:35:39,055 --> 00:35:43,418
I am here to look for someone.

396
00:35:44,328 --> 00:35:45,539
Have you found the person?

397
00:35:48,832 --> 00:35:50,251
I am still looking for the person.

398
00:35:52,480 --> 00:35:54,324
To charge your cell phone,

399
00:35:54,324 --> 00:35:56,637
could you come to the front desk now?
I will be waiting for you.

400
00:35:57,587 --> 00:36:00,158
Okay, I will come now.

401
00:36:00,158 --> 00:36:01,419
It won't take long.

402
00:36:38,735 --> 00:36:39,763
Hello?

403
00:36:41,289 --> 00:36:42,397
Hello?

404
00:36:43,336 --> 00:36:44,858
Yes, this is he.

405
00:36:47,391 --> 00:36:48,391
What?

406
00:36:51,791 --> 00:36:52,795
Okay.

407
00:36:54,967 --> 00:36:57,682
I am sorry. Please go to the airport.

408
00:37:10,586 --> 00:37:11,827
Is she all right?

409
00:37:13,081 --> 00:37:14,369
Is she okay?

410
00:37:14,369 --> 00:37:15,941
What is going on?

411
00:37:16,818 --> 00:37:19,944
She barely ate anything
because you were not coming back.

412
00:37:19,944 --> 00:37:21,356
Now, look at her.

413
00:37:24,657 --> 00:37:25,786
I am sorry.

414
00:38:15,937 --> 00:38:17,132
Hello?

415
00:38:44,313 --> 00:38:46,709
I am sorry. I did not know you came back.

416
00:38:47,329 --> 00:38:48,427
Don't leave.

417
00:39:02,241 --> 00:39:03,947
It is great that you came.

418
00:39:05,161 --> 00:39:07,093
I was going to call you.

419
00:39:08,977 --> 00:39:10,956
Do you need something?

420
00:39:14,176 --> 00:39:16,740
Don't be too formal.

421
00:39:21,082 --> 00:39:25,339
You are pretty.

422
00:39:28,208 --> 00:39:29,643
It is interesting.

423
00:39:31,977 --> 00:39:33,967
Is there something wrong with my vision?

424
00:39:36,033 --> 00:39:37,321
What are you doing?

425
00:39:40,456 --> 00:39:41,739
What am I doing?

426
00:39:50,065 --> 00:39:52,004
Do you mean why am I drinking?

427
00:39:56,040 --> 00:39:57,391
I...

428
00:40:00,052 --> 00:40:01,600
Because...

429
00:40:04,749 --> 00:40:06,611
You do not need to tell me
if it is something personal.

430
00:40:06,611 --> 00:40:07,764
Excuse me.

431
00:40:07,764 --> 00:40:08,983
I'm celebrating a wedding.

432
00:40:14,571 --> 00:40:17,639
My mother in Japan got married again.

433
00:40:19,396 --> 00:40:22,598
Is this the third time or the fourth?

434
00:40:26,489 --> 00:40:31,539
If I count Dad,
this would be the fifth wedding.

435
00:40:35,337 --> 00:40:38,898
You said you were going
to your mother's birthday dinner.

436
00:40:40,914 --> 00:40:41,914
Did I?

437
00:40:44,849 --> 00:40:46,610
I have two mothers.

438
00:40:48,169 --> 00:40:50,592
One is my biological mother, who left me.

439
00:40:50,592 --> 00:40:55,763
The other is the mother of my brothers
who totally ignore me.

440
00:40:57,162 --> 00:40:58,508
Our madam.

441
00:41:03,361 --> 00:41:06,491
Why am I telling you all this?

442
00:41:09,257 --> 00:41:12,282
What are you?

443
00:41:13,914 --> 00:41:15,132
Who are you?

444
00:41:18,534 --> 00:41:21,434
All right.

445
00:41:25,063 --> 00:41:26,620
I know why.

446
00:41:28,895 --> 00:41:30,770
I am really interested in you.

447
00:41:34,223 --> 00:41:38,666
You have something against me
since I told you all my secrets.

448
00:41:41,715 --> 00:41:43,445
I am sorry. Excuse me.

449
00:41:49,891 --> 00:41:51,238
Will you be my girlfriend?

450
00:41:53,770 --> 00:41:56,135
Go out with me.

451
00:41:58,676 --> 00:42:01,511
I will behave. I will try.

452
00:42:01,511 --> 00:42:03,060
I will do anything for you.

453
00:42:05,102 --> 00:42:06,206
Excuse me.

454
00:42:06,206 --> 00:42:07,800
Stop there. Stop.

455
00:43:20,815 --> 00:43:21,823
Hello.

456
00:43:22,406 --> 00:43:24,447
Hello, is there anyone who paged me?

457
00:43:25,349 --> 00:43:28,841
I did. It is the friend of Han Tae Seok.

458
00:43:29,908 --> 00:43:33,327
I see. I wonder who it was.

459
00:43:34,198 --> 00:43:36,432
I am sorry that I made you wait.

460
00:43:38,494 --> 00:43:42,189
I am truly sorry. I had something urgent.

461
00:43:42,189 --> 00:43:43,600
I am in Seoul now.

462
00:43:44,924 --> 00:43:46,382
My friend...

463
00:43:49,531 --> 00:43:51,591
My friend got sick, so...

464
00:43:52,044 --> 00:43:53,694
I see.

465
00:43:54,188 --> 00:43:56,478
It happens. Don't worry about it.

466
00:44:02,187 --> 00:44:04,591
I actually...

467
00:44:06,397 --> 00:44:08,421
I knew who paged me.

468
00:44:10,963 --> 00:44:15,069
But I got annoyed a little.

469
00:44:15,069 --> 00:44:16,880
So, I ignored it.

470
00:44:19,014 --> 00:44:20,766
I waited quite a long time.

471
00:44:24,109 --> 00:44:28,896
So, I even stopped by your room
minutes ago.

472
00:44:37,950 --> 00:44:40,888
I remember your cell phone number.

473
00:44:43,438 --> 00:44:47,819
You have the same last digits as mine,
so I memorized it.

474
00:44:47,819 --> 00:44:49,110
Your number is 0215.

475
00:44:52,875 --> 00:44:54,006
It is the date of a birthday.

476
00:44:55,571 --> 00:44:58,908
For me too, it is a birthday.

477
00:45:02,232 --> 00:45:04,092
Anyway, I'm sorry for making you wait.

478
00:45:05,200 --> 00:45:06,767
It is all right.

479
00:45:06,767 --> 00:45:09,154
I am glad you are okay,
and not in an accident or something.

480
00:45:13,698 --> 00:45:17,456
Are you all right? You do not sound...

481
00:45:17,456 --> 00:45:19,169
I am fine.

482
00:45:19,169 --> 00:45:21,442
It's because of the rain.

483
00:45:21,442 --> 00:45:23,221
The connection is not that good, right?

484
00:45:26,506 --> 00:45:29,566
You must have returned without meeting
the person you were looking for.

485
00:45:30,849 --> 00:45:31,849
Yes.

486
00:45:35,713 --> 00:45:37,892
I think I have been mistaken.

487
00:45:41,472 --> 00:45:43,012
Because I missed her so much.

488
00:45:47,714 --> 00:45:51,238
I miss her so much that
I would mistake someone for her.

489
00:45:51,238 --> 00:45:52,313
I see.

490
00:45:54,734 --> 00:45:56,519
It was someone you missed that much.

491
00:46:04,150 --> 00:46:05,663
Okay, then.

492
00:46:05,663 --> 00:46:06,896
Hello.

493
00:46:08,469 --> 00:46:10,359
Whose birthday is it?

494
00:46:11,265 --> 00:46:12,265
What?

495
00:46:12,265 --> 00:46:13,397
I meant your pager number.

496
00:46:18,766 --> 00:46:20,392
It is my brother's birthday.

497
00:46:22,590 --> 00:46:23,857
Whose birthday is it?

498
00:46:25,366 --> 00:46:26,592
It is my birthday.

499
00:46:30,190 --> 00:46:31,190
Okay.

500
00:46:34,750 --> 00:46:35,913
All right.

501
00:46:36,894 --> 00:46:39,193
Please visit our villa again, sir.

502
00:46:40,958 --> 00:46:41,958
I will.

503
00:47:15,515 --> 00:47:16,825
What should I do?

504
00:47:16,825 --> 00:47:21,970
Yu Mi, you sit still just like a painting.

505
00:47:21,970 --> 00:47:23,808
Am I not helpful?

506
00:47:23,808 --> 00:47:26,267
I will organize paintings, then.

507
00:47:27,983 --> 00:47:32,161
The painting organizes paintings.

508
00:47:33,920 --> 00:47:36,320
Will it be all right to organize them
the way I like, Jun Seo?

509
00:47:36,320 --> 00:47:37,475
Sure.

510
00:47:39,087 --> 00:47:41,638
Is it far from here, this beach?

511
00:47:41,638 --> 00:47:44,016
No, it's not. It's close.

512
00:47:44,016 --> 00:47:45,639
Do you want to go there later?

513
00:47:45,639 --> 00:47:47,770
You should draw me.

514
00:47:48,054 --> 00:47:49,057
Come in.

515
00:47:52,727 --> 00:47:54,122
Did you ask for me, sir?

516
00:47:54,988 --> 00:47:55,988
Yes.

517
00:47:58,310 --> 00:48:01,753
What happened to Choi Eun Seo?

518
00:48:02,214 --> 00:48:03,478
Yes, sir.

519
00:48:03,478 --> 00:48:07,318
Choi Eun Seo quit
because of an absurd guest.

520
00:48:07,318 --> 00:48:08,808
She is absent without notice.

521
00:48:09,837 --> 00:48:13,729
She is probably on a blind date
with a middle-aged man.

522
00:48:14,373 --> 00:48:15,743
A middle-aged man?

523
00:48:15,743 --> 00:48:18,076
She is being sold off.

524
00:48:18,076 --> 00:48:22,226
If you do not need anything,
can I leave before getting fired?

525
00:48:24,582 --> 00:48:26,448
Wait.

526
00:48:55,078 --> 00:48:58,495
Be nice to him.

527
00:48:58,495 --> 00:49:01,038
It's good that mom isn't home.

528
00:49:01,038 --> 00:49:02,639
If she had been here...

529
00:49:02,639 --> 00:49:04,193
I'm sick of that.

530
00:49:11,840 --> 00:49:13,355
Hello, President Kim.

531
00:49:14,247 --> 00:49:15,247
You are here.

532
00:49:17,985 --> 00:49:19,338
Please get in the car.

533
00:49:19,338 --> 00:49:20,500
Get in the car, now.

534
00:49:21,658 --> 00:49:24,317
- You get in first, sir.
- All right, then.

535
00:49:27,163 --> 00:49:28,206
President Kim.

536
00:49:34,499 --> 00:49:35,740
I apologize.

537
00:49:57,297 --> 00:49:59,369
You missed work without notice,

538
00:49:59,369 --> 00:50:00,783
and you're on a blind date
with that old man.

539
00:50:02,321 --> 00:50:03,811
Who made this happen?

540
00:50:08,594 --> 00:50:09,940
I don't want to argue with you.

541
00:50:11,129 --> 00:50:13,786
Acts of arguing and blaming you hurt me,
and I hate that.

542
00:50:18,914 --> 00:50:23,473
I have listened to you
complaining about your life,

543
00:50:23,473 --> 00:50:24,965
so now it's your turn.

544
00:50:28,386 --> 00:50:29,508
I...

545
00:50:31,426 --> 00:50:36,225
My family was deeply in debt
and ran away so many times.

546
00:50:36,225 --> 00:50:37,934
And every time we ran away,
we owed money again.

547
00:50:40,810 --> 00:50:42,324
My brother is a gangster.

548
00:50:43,003 --> 00:50:46,120
He hurt his hand from fighting,
so he can't work anymore.

549
00:50:48,942 --> 00:50:53,269
After he got injured, my mom...

550
00:50:53,269 --> 00:50:55,033
lost the will to live.

551
00:50:57,375 --> 00:50:59,602
So we make ends meet with my payroll.

552
00:51:04,494 --> 00:51:07,369
But I quit my job now,
so what am I supposed to do?

553
00:51:09,971 --> 00:51:12,515
That old man likes me.

554
00:51:12,515 --> 00:51:14,414
He would buy me if I agreed to it.

555
00:51:15,811 --> 00:51:18,973
That is enough. I should be grateful.

556
00:51:19,664 --> 00:51:21,436
Right?

557
00:51:21,436 --> 00:51:22,436
Aren't I right?

558
00:51:23,131 --> 00:51:24,133
How much are you?

559
00:51:26,235 --> 00:51:28,643
How much are you worth? I will buy you.

560
00:51:28,643 --> 00:51:30,126
I will pay you more.

561
00:51:34,290 --> 00:51:35,477
This beach,

562
00:51:37,115 --> 00:51:39,974
this place is more than anything for me
with precious memories.

563
00:51:42,203 --> 00:51:46,191
I'm so sad to be here with someone
like you, even for a minute.

564
00:51:49,754 --> 00:51:51,189
I don't want to see you ever again.
